including the attribution and noncommercial conditions.

MRI segmentation data
---------------------
The numerical study uses an anonymized, preprocessed HDF5 subset. Raw MRI
volumes, masks, MRI case-image figures and their source filenames are not
distributed. Release-local case aliases preserve pairing across numeric
tables. Exact mapping to the public challenge release and complete upstream
conversion provenance remain unavailable; the measured subset must not be
presented as the complete official challenge benchmark.

Libraries and scientific references
-----------------------------------
PyTorch, torchvision, NumPy, SciPy, scikit-learn, h5py, MedPy, Matplotlib,
Pillow, PyYAML, nibabel, PyMuPDF, pytest and TeX remain subject to their own
licenses. ImageNet-pretrained backbone weights are downloaded by torchvision
and are not included. Model and metric references are in SOURCES.md and the
research manuscript. No third-party code, pretrained checkpoint binary or
downloaded reference paper is bundled.
